# Thomas Test Suite Project

This is a Thomas test project initialized with `thomas init`.

## Quick Start

### 1. Configure Environment

Copy the example environment and add your API base URL:

```bash
cp config/environments/example.json.dist config/environments/example.json
# Edit config/environments/example.json and set your api_base_url
```

### 2. Add Test Scenarios

Create test scenario files in the `scenarios/` directory:

```bash
cat > scenarios/my_test.json << 'EOF'
{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "feature": "my_feature",
  "description": "Test my feature",
  "request": {
    "method": "POST",
    "path": "/api/endpoint",
    "body": {}
  },
  "api_checks": [
    {
      "path": "status_code",
      "operator": "equals",
      "expected": 200
    }
  ],
  "validations": []
}
EOF
```

### 3. Run Tests

```bash
thomas request \
  --environment config/environments/example.json \
  --folder scenarios \
  --variables config/variables.example.json
```

### 4. Generate Report

```bash
thomas report execution-record.json
```

## Examples

For learning Thomas patterns, check the `examples/` folder:

```bash
# Start the mock server
python examples/mock_server.py &

# Run example scenarios
thomas request \
  --environment examples/config/environments/example.json \
  --folder examples/scenarios \
  --variables examples/config/variables.example.json

# Generate example report
thomas report execution-record.json
```

## Project Structure

- `scenarios/` — Your test scenarios (JSON files)
- `config/environments/` — Environment configurations (credentials, base URLs)
- `config/variables.example.json` — Shared test variables
- `examples/` — Reference implementations and mock server for learning
- `.gitignore` — Recommended ignores (customize as needed)

## Documentation

For more information, see the [Thomas Test Suite documentation](https://github.com/serjupla/the-thomas-test-suite).
